From: leopard-webkit-build
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: detect target arch from CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES on Apple

On Apple cross-builds CMake's platform init (triggered by project())
overwrites CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR with the *host* arch (e.g. arm64 on
Apple Silicon) even when -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR=x86_64 is passed.
That corrupts the WTF_CPU detection in the top-level CMakeLists.txt:
WTF_CPU_ARM gets set for an x86_64 target, which in turn makes the JSC
LLInt backend selection fall through to ARMv7_TRADITIONAL. The offlineasm
then emits an ARM interpreter into an x86_64 binary, so LLIntOffsetsExtractor
has no matching configuration and the generated extractorTable is empty —
producing "offlineasm: No magic values found" and aborting the JSC build.

CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES reliably carries the real target arch, so prefer
it when present. Tested on an Apple-Silicon -> macOS 10.6 x86_64 build.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,15 @@
 # since the later one just resolves to the host processor on Windows.
 if (MSVC_CXX_ARCHITECTURE_ID)
     string(TOLOWER ${MSVC_CXX_ARCHITECTURE_ID} LOWERCASE_CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR)
+elseif (APPLE AND CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES)
+    # [leopard-webkit-build] On Apple cross-builds CMake's platform init overwrites
+    # CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR with the *host* arch (e.g. arm64 on Apple Silicon),
+    # which corrupts the WTF_CPU detection below and the JSC LLInt backend selection
+    # that depends on it (it generated an ARMv7_TRADITIONAL LLInt for an x86_64 target).
+    # CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES carries the real target arch, so prefer it here.
+    list(GET CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES 0 _WEBKIT_OSX_FIRST_ARCH)
+    string(TOLOWER "${_WEBKIT_OSX_FIRST_ARCH}" LOWERCASE_CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR)
+    unset(_WEBKIT_OSX_FIRST_ARCH)
 else ()
     string(TOLOWER ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} LOWERCASE_CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR)
 endif ()
